message: "If you use or refer to this software or research platform, please cite it as below."
title: "Malbolge: C-to-Malbolge compiler and compiler-algorithm research platform"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Villa Osorno"
    given-names: "Alberto"
date-released: "2026-07-26"
url: "https://github.com/albertovillaosorno/malbolge"
repository-code: "https://github.com/albertovillaosorno/malbolge"
license: MIT
# The citation date is intentionally frozen. It is the stable publication epoch
# for the living Git repository, not a moving last-modified timestamp. Future
# commits do not rewrite citations already used by readers.
abstract: >-
  Malbolge is an experimental C-to-Malbolge compiler, execution, verification,
  and reproducible compiler-research platform built around the 1998 Malbolge
  machine. The written 1998 specification is normative when it disagrees with
  the historical C interpreter. The project investigates deterministic C
  lowering, exact virtual machines, translation validation, mathematical
  optimization, stochastic and guided superoptimization, replaceable CPU/GPU
  accelerator adapters, tiered native AOT/JIT execution, parametric compiler
  challenge families, and eventual self-hosting.
keywords:
  - malbolge
  - compilers
  - compiler research
  - superoptimization
  - program synthesis
  - translation validation
  - self-modifying code
  - ternary computing
  - just-in-time compilation
  - gpu computing
  - reproducible research
